Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
September 2, 2025
Thompson
Excused:
Further Business
18. Consideration of a resolution to rescind amendment two (250819-15)
to the cooperative agreement (200218-02) between Laramie County,
WY, and the WY Dept of Transportation County.
25 - 411
Resolution, Rescinding Amendment Two to the
Cooperative Agreement
Attachments:
Molly Cook, Public Works, requested that the board rescind an amendment approved
on Aug 19, 2025. She noted WYDOT has not signed it. Cook spoke about a meeting
that was held between the county, city of Cheyenne, and WYDOT on Aug 26, 2025.
She said an agreement will be brought back at a later date to be signed concurrently
with a memorandum of understanding. She said the MOU will consolidate and define
reimbursement costs between the county and the city.
A motion was made by Commissioner Zwonitzer, seconded by
Commissioner Hollingshead, to rescind the county's approval at this time.
The motion carried by the following vote:
Malm, Heath, Hollingshead, Zwonitzer
Aye:
Thompson
Excused:
19. Consideration of a resolution reappointing Mark T Voss as the
Laramie County Attorney in accordance with WS 18-3-301(a)
effective Sept 1, 2025.
25 - 409
Resolution Reappointing County Attorney Mark T Voss
Attachments:
A motion was made by Commissioner Hollingshead, seconded by
Commissioner Zwonitzer, to reappoint Mark T Voss. The motion carried by
the following vote:
Malm, Heath, Hollingshead, Zwonitzer
Aye:
Thompson
Excused:
The meeting adjourned at 3:51 pm.
